                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "401f232a-4cdc-376c-9172-992d1cc7af68",
                        "entry_id": "d1a738c2-2572-325e-9963-93b037b39a20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een staat die veiligheid, rust en het materieel- en geestelijk welbevinden van haar burgers als haar verantwoordelijkheid stelt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2cfb43b-efe6-4c7a-84fb-8dcc154c673a",
                                "sense_id": "401f232a-4cdc-376c-9172-992d1cc7af68",
                                "text": "De grote golfbewegingen in maatschappij en economie vormen een altijd weer terugkerend patroon van actie en reactie. Iedere trend ontaardt uiteindelijk in excessen en roept tegenkrachten op. Dat gebeurde in de jaren zeventig, toen de welvaartsstaat ontspoorde en dat gebeurt nu weer, nu dertig jaar marktwerking heel veel achterblijvers blijkt te hebben opgeleverd. Die laten met steeds luider stem van zich horen. Zij bepalen de uitslagen van verkiezingen en referenda."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1efc2d34-e08a-4a15-943c-324fd7d49297",
                                "sense_id": "401f232a-4cdc-376c-9172-992d1cc7af68",
                                "text": "We vergeten nog wel eens dat onze welvaartsstaat en onze democratie in Europa voor een belangrijk deel wortels hebben in de oorlog."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "37f0c19d-0592-44bb-974e-12e956d6aa2d",
                        "source_entry_id": "d1a738c2-2572-325e-9963-93b037b39a20",
                        "source_sense_id": "401f232a-4cdc-376c-9172-992d1cc7af68",
                        "target_lang_word": "welfare state",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "welfare state",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "453f6870-9dfe-3d59-aaf5-deef278cccfb",
                                        "entry_id": "eebfbaa5-b56a-3004-bfbb-88ebdffa3005",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A social system in which the state takes overall responsibility for the welfare of its citizens, providing health care, education, unemployment benefits and social security."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35d65043-5f2c-4176-9422-272d80692004",
                                                "sense_id": "453f6870-9dfe-3d59-aaf5-deef278cccfb",
                                                "text": "In order to grant the rich these pleasures, the social contract is reconfigured. The welfare state is dismantled. Essential public services are cut so that the rich may pay less tax. […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f18bff43-11ce-4e4d-a668-e05c2466bfb0",
                                                "sense_id": "453f6870-9dfe-3d59-aaf5-deef278cccfb",
                                                "text": "Wagenknecht […] argues further that a policy of high migration enforces a minimal welfare state that is ‘cheaper for the upper and upper middle classes in comparison to a real welfare state, but it is not an attractive project for the middle and lower middle groups. Thus, if one wants to remove support for social provisions, this is exactly the way to do it’."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ab0e353-451e-36ec-b085-93da38ca39d8",
                                        "entry_id": "eebfbaa5-b56a-3004-bfbb-88ebdffa3005",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A country in which such a system operates."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
